=== .numinance/policy/autonomy.yaml ===
# AutonomyPolicy "pr-only", written by "numi init". The ladder level is AUTONOMY_LEVEL_PR: the agent may open pull requests
# and may never merge. (PR_ONLY is a breaker state of the engine, not a ladder level; this document is the ladder side.)
apiVersion: numinance.dev/v1
kind: AutonomyPolicy
metadata: {name: pr-only, scope: SCOPE_REPO}
# The extensions block holds the confidence of each drafted value (high, medium or low) and the evidence
# that showed it. The Engine never reads it. Written by "numi discover"; review each value before merging.
extensions:
  dev.numinance.discover:
    spec.defaults.level: {confidence: high, evidence: "fixed by numi discover, not discovered"}
spec:
  defaults: {level: AUTONOMY_LEVEL_PR}
  # No floors block: a floor set below the org scope is refused. When no org document sets floors the engine applies its
  # shipped floor (at most SUGGEST for HIGH risk and above, at most PR for the rest), which caps every change at PR.
  # Run "numi init --org-dir DIR" to write an explicit floors block into an organization policy repository.
=== .numinance/policy/playbook-bugfix-bounded.yaml ===
# Playbook "bugfix-bounded", written by "numi init": a bounded bug fix that ends in a pull request. The verifier names are
# the ones of the LanguageToolchain python-3.12.
apiVersion: numinance.dev/v1
kind: Playbook
metadata: {name: bugfix-bounded, scope: SCOPE_REPO}
# The extensions block holds the confidence of each drafted value (high, medium or low) and the evidence
# that showed it. The Engine never reads it. Written by "numi discover"; review each value before merging.
extensions:
  dev.numinance.discover:
    spec.steps.fix.verifiers: {confidence: high, evidence: "pyproject.toml [tool.ruff]"}
spec:
  change_type: bugfix
  steps:
    # One step per identity kind. The capability_set names are the ones the deployment defines: implement (author-agent:
    # the branch push and the pull request), review (reviewer-agent: verifier.run), release (release-pipeline: the read-only
    # status of the pull request). No step merges: Numinance opens pull requests only.
    - {name: fix, capability_set: implement, risk: RISK_CLASS_MEDIUM, evidence: [diff, pr-ref], verifiers: [lint]}
    - {name: review, capability_set: review, risk: RISK_CLASS_LOW}
    - {name: pr-status, capability_set: release, risk: RISK_CLASS_LOW}
  max_repair_attempts: 2
  qualification: {min_runs: 20, max_rework_rate: 1000, max_regression_rate: 0, max_rollback_rate: 50, zero_security_escapes: true}
=== .numinance/policy/sdlc-profile.yaml ===
# SDLCProfile of this repository, written by "numi init". It binds the names defined in this tree
# (or granted by the organization policy repository) to this repository.
#
# CI: github-actions
#   github-actions: the ciexecutor provider dev.numinance.ci-github-actions exists in the open plugins (replay and live builds).
#   It starts a workflow_dispatch workflow that the repository already defines on its default branch
#   (the README of that provider says what the workflow must declare). A live run is not yet verified.
apiVersion: numinance.dev/v1
kind: SDLCProfile
metadata: {name: python-repo, scope: SCOPE_REPO}
# The extensions block holds the confidence of each drafted value (high, medium or low) and the evidence
# that showed it. The Engine never reads it. Written by "numi discover"; review each value before merging.
extensions:
  dev.numinance.discover:
    spec.toolchains: {confidence: low, evidence: "default, no version found"}
    spec.adapters.ciexecutor: {confidence: high, evidence: ".github/workflows/ok.yml"}
    spec.adapters.scm: {confidence: low, evidence: "default, github is the only provider that exists"}
spec:
  playbooks: [bugfix-bounded]
  toolchains: [python-3.12]
  adapters:
    scm: {provider: dev.numinance.scm-github, instance: main}
    ciexecutor: {provider: dev.numinance.ci-github-actions, instance: ci}
=== .numinance/policy/stage-registry.yaml ===
# StageRegistry "pr-only", written by "numi init": the stage names of this repository mapped onto the fixed Change state
# machine. The registry names no stage for the Merging state, so no stage of it can merge; the last stage is the human
# pr-gate. Each CI system has its own verify stage. Only the org scope selects a registry
# (SDLCProfile.stages), so below the org this registry is defined but not selected.
apiVersion: numinance.dev/v1
kind: StageRegistry
metadata: {name: pr-only, scope: SCOPE_REPO}
# The extensions block holds the confidence of each drafted value (high, medium or low) and the evidence
# that showed it. The Engine never reads it. Written by "numi discover"; review each value before merging.
extensions:
  dev.numinance.discover:
    spec.stages.ci: {confidence: high, evidence: ".github/workflows/ok.yml"}
spec:
  stages:
    - {name: triage, maps_to: CHANGE_STATE_CLASSIFIED}
    - {name: plan-review, maps_to: CHANGE_STATE_PLAN_GATE, gate: {kind: GATE_KIND_PLAN}, requires: [triage]}
    - {name: implement, maps_to: CHANGE_STATE_IMPLEMENTING, requires: [plan-review]}
    # Static checks run by the verifier provider on the candidate.
    - {name: verify-static, maps_to: CHANGE_STATE_VERIFYING, requires: [implement]}
    # GitHub Actions: runs the repository's own workflow through the ciexecutor port.
    - {name: ci-github-actions, maps_to: CHANGE_STATE_VERIFYING, requires: [verify-static]}
    - name: pr-gate
      maps_to: CHANGE_STATE_RELEASE_GATE
      gate:
        kind: GATE_KIND_HUMAN
        approver_role: maintainer
        sod: {distinct_from: [author-agent, reviewer-agent]}
        required_approvals: 1
      requires: [ci-github-actions]
=== .numinance/policy/toolchain-python.yaml ===
# LanguageToolchain for Python, written by "numi init". The toolchain is explicit: language, version, package manager and
# the verifier set are the values chosen by the flags of "numi init" or detected in the repository; edit them here.
# The verifier provider takes the check to run in "config.check". It may also take "settings", the text of the tool's own
# settings file (ruff.toml, mypy.ini, pytest.ini); it never reads settings files of the candidate.
apiVersion: numinance.dev/v1
kind: LanguageToolchain
metadata: {name: python-3.12, scope: SCOPE_REPO}
# The extensions block holds the confidence of each drafted value (high, medium or low) and the evidence
# that showed it. The Engine never reads it. Written by "numi discover"; review each value before merging.
extensions:
  dev.numinance.discover:
    spec.language: {confidence: medium, evidence: "1 python files in the bounded walk"}
    spec.version: {confidence: low, evidence: "default, no version found"}
    spec.package_manager: {confidence: low, evidence: "pyproject.toml with no package manager table, the default"}
    spec.verifiers.lint: {confidence: high, evidence: "pyproject.toml [tool.ruff]"}
spec:
  language: python
  version: "3.12"
  verifiers:
    - {name: lint, provider: dev.numinance.verifier-python, config: {check: ruff, timeout_seconds: 60}}
  package_manager: uv
=== PULL_REQUEST.md ===
Add the Numinance configuration drafted by numi discover

## What this adds

A draft `.numinance/` for this repository, written by `numi discover` from the enforcement artifacts the repository already has (files only; nothing was executed). Autonomy is PR only: the agent may open pull requests and may never merge. Nothing in this pull request merges anything.

## What was discovered

- source files: python 1
- github-actions workflows: ok.yml
- ruff in pyproject.toml [tool.ruff]
- no default branch recorded in .git (no clone metadata)
- skipped while walking: 2 links, 1 hidden entries, directories none
- commands a person runs for these tools: lint uv run ruff check

## Confidence

Each drafted value carries its confidence and evidence under `extensions` (`dev.numinance.discover`) in its document. High: a settings file, a pyproject table, a lockfile or a version file. Medium: a dependency listing, a requires-python bound, a section of another file or a workflow with workflow_dispatch. Low: only a use in a hook, requirements or CI text, the current branch, or a default taken because nothing was found.

| Decision | Value | Confidence | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| package manager | uv | low | pyproject.toml with no package manager table, the default |
| python | 3.12 | low | default, no version found |
| language | python | medium | 1 python files in the bounded walk |
| verifier lint | ruff | high | pyproject.toml [tool.ruff] |
| ci | github-actions | high | .github/workflows/ok.yml |
| scm | github | low | default, github is the only provider that exists |
| tickets | none | low | default, no ticketing provider exists yet |
| default branch | none | low | no clone metadata in .git |
| CODEOWNERS | none found | low | no CODEOWNERS file |
| autonomy | PR only | high | fixed by numi discover, not discovered |

## Self-test

- HEAD not resolved (no readable .git/HEAD: not a git repository, a gitfile or a worktree)
- 5 drafted documents decoded by the kind loader (schema and loader checks)
- a second read of the repository gave the same decisions and the same HEAD
- every verifier in the draft has evidence

## Reviewer checklist

- [ ] Every row of low confidence is read against the repository and corrected or accepted on purpose.
- [ ] The verifiers, the Python version and the package manager match how the repository really runs its checks.
- [ ] The CI binding names the workflow the repository uses, and that workflow declares workflow_dispatch on the default branch.
- [ ] `.numinance/policy/**` is protected with a CODEOWNERS rule (for example `/.numinance/policy/ @your-org/security`) and branch protection that requires that owner's review, so agents cannot change their own gates.
- [ ] Nothing in this pull request merges anything: the autonomy level is PR only and the pull request needs a human approval like any other.
- [ ] The confidence annotations under `extensions` are kept or removed as the team prefers; the Engine never reads them.
